  "subject": "a young man in Jayapura who secretly practises yospan steps in his kitchen with a broom as his partner so he can dance with Martha at her sister's graduation party, and on the night still starts on the wrong foot until she counts for him",
  "caption": "Papuan yospan dance-pop, modern eastern-Indonesian party style rooted in yosim pancar. Tifa hand drums driving a skipping two-step pattern, fast ukulele strum, bouncing electric bass on the offbeats, bright clean electric guitar riff, hand claps and group call-and-response shouts. Bright bouncy mix, outdoor-party feel. Warm male mid-register vocal, playful, with a friendly group answering lines. 128 BPM, C major. Mood of a nervous young man laughing at himself on the dance floor. No dangdut kendang, no EDM drop, no trap hi-hats, no autotune, no slow ballad section.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro - tifa drums, ukulele strum, claps]\n[Verse 1]\nMalam-malam di dapur mama\nSa dansa dengan sapu lidi\nKiri, kanan, putar badan\nSapu jatuh, sa tertawa sendiri\n[Pre-Chorus]\nSabtu nanti pesta wisuda\nMartha pasti datang juga\n[Chorus]\nKo pu kaki kiri, sa pu kaki kanan\nYospan pelan-pelan, jangan dulu lari\nTifa su bunyi, semua berdiri\nMartha senyum, sa salah kaki\n[Verse 2]\nLampu warna di halaman\nMartha tarik sa ke tengah\nSa mulai dengan kaki kanan\nSemua orang tahan tawa\n[Chorus]\nKo pu kaki kiri, sa pu kaki kanan\nMartha hitung satu, dua, tiga\nTifa su bunyi, semua berdiri\nSekarang sa tra salah lagi\n[Outro - group shouts, tifa ends]\nSapu lidi di dapur mama\nTra sa pakai lagi, ee",
